================================================================================
astro4j / JSol'Ex
================================================================================

Portions of SolScan's spectral-line identification, exposure calculation, and SHG reconstruction
logic are translated and adapted from the astro4j project (JSol'Ex, JSol'Ex CLI, jsolex-core),
by Cedric Champeau ("melix") and contributors.
    https://melix.github.io/blog/2023/04-22-introducing-astro4j.html

Licensed under the Apache License, Version 2.0. A copy of the License is available at:
    http://www.apache.org/licenses/LICENSE-2.0

astro4j does not ship a NOTICE file of its own to propagate. Per-file attribution is instead
retained in the header of each SolScan source file that closely translates a specific astro4j
source file, pointing back to the original.

Specifically adapted, at time of writing (see CLAUDE.md for the full, current list):
  - DeepLineIdentifier (spectral line identification via reference-atlas correlation)
  - SpectralLineCatalog (interesting-lines.txt secondary-line lookup)
  - SpectrumBrowser (dispersion-aware reference-spectrum rendering)
  - ExposureCalculator (recommended exposure/fps from instrument optics and solar ephemeris)
  - SpectroHeliograph / Setup (equipment-profile data shapes)
  - SolexVideoProcessor and related workflow steps (SHG reconstruction pipeline)

